\begin{frame}{5.2 ATE computation outline}\evidence{PLANNED / no gate PASS}
Absolute Trajectory Error (ATE) compares associated poses after a declared alignment. $P_i$ is the estimate and $Q_i$ the reference; root mean square error (RMSE) summarizes translation [8].\par\medskip\coursefigure{D70}{\begin{tikzpicture}[y=.8cm,font=\normalsize,box/.append style={font=\normalsize}]\node[box,text width=165mm] {$E_i=Q_i^{-1}SP_i,\qquad e_i=\|\operatorname{trans}(E_i)\|,\qquad \mathrm{RMSE}=\sqrt{\frac{1}{N}\sum_i e_i^2}$};\end{tikzpicture}}{Rigid alignment S removes reference-origin choice, not a stereo scale error.}\par\medskip Associate epochs within a predeclared tolerance; retain unmatched samples. Convert both trajectories to the same pose direction and units before fitting $S$. Report valid overlap and failure trials.\vfill\takeaway{In Figure~\ref{fig:D70}, without independent reference data, D435i absolute accuracy stays UNKNOWN.}\note{Source: docs/ORB\_SLAM3\_OFFLINE\_PREPARATION.md; upstream pinned stereo\_inertial\_euroc.cc; evo Metrics. Commands are teaching examples only; none executed. UNKNOWN budgets require approval.}\end{frame}
\begin{frame}{5.3 RPE and pair policy}\evidence{CALCULATED N4A / no gate PASS}
Relative Pose Error (RPE) compares estimated motion with reference motion over a declared interval [8].\par\medskip\coursefigure{D71}{\begin{tikzpicture}[y=.8cm,font=\normalsize,box/.append style={font=\normalsize}]\node[box,text width=165mm] {$E_{ij}=(Q_i^{-1}Q_j)^{-1}(P_i^{-1}P_j)$\\Translation and rotation are separate metrics.};\end{tikzpicture}}{Relative deltas expose local drift rather than global alignment choice.}\par\par\begin{tabular}{@{}L{83mm}L{101mm}@{}}\toprule
\textbf{Pair policy} & \textbf{Question answered}\\\midrule
Fixed time separation & How wrong is motion over that duration?\\[6pt]
Fixed distance separation & How does error grow per traveled distance?\\[6pt]
Consecutive vs all eligible pairs & Different weighting; report choice and pair count\\[6pt]
\bottomrule\end{tabular}\par\vfill\takeaway{In Figure~\ref{fig:D71}, never compare RPE numbers with different delta units or pairing policies.}\note{Evidence: slides\_course/qa/n4a-traj-eval-summary.md; tools/trajectory\_eval/README.md. CALCULATED using traj\_eval.py from claude/project-thread-upkfjv, commit d3f9540, PR 2; tool not yet merged. Tool validation passed per its README, not rerun by this deck task. Flags: --t-max-diff 0.02 --t-offset 0 --align-both --rotation-ate --rpe-delta 1 --rpe-unit s. Shared EuRoC clock assumed; offset zero; active body-to-world poses in imu\_body, metres. 3,639 timestamp-associated pose pairs per run. For each eligible start, choose the first later reference timestamp at least 1 s later; no interpolation. SE(3) rigid alignment cancels in RPE. The tool's SE(3) ATE reproduces saved evo scores; its RPE pair policy differs from evo filters. Sim(3) additionally fits scale and is diagnostic, not the stereo-inertial paper comparator. Does not establish frames, extrinsics, synchronization, sensor readiness or gate PASS. No new camera, Pi or ORB execution. Source: evo Metrics [8]. Commands are teaching examples only; none executed. UNKNOWN budgets require approval.}\end{frame}
\begin{frame}{5.4 Trajectory conversion and evo}\evidence{PLANNED / no gate PASS}
\begin{block}{Future commands / tools}{\ttfamily\normalsize evo\_ape tum REFERENCE.tum ESTIMATE.tum --align\par evo\_rpe tum REFERENCE.tum ESTIMATE.tum \textbackslash{}\par \quad --pose\_relation angle\_deg --delta 1 --delta\_unit m}\end{block}\medskip The 1 m delta is a command example, not a project acceptance threshold [8]. Check installed --help, version, association tolerance, valid coverage and reference quality.\begin{block}{Conversion before comparison}Technical University of Munich (TUM) format uses seconds, xyz and quaternion qx qy qz qw. Preserve EuRoC originals; audit quaternion order, units, pose direction and frame. Metric stereo defaults to rigid alignment; scale fitting is a separate diagnostic.\end{block}\vfill\takeaway{Store exact argv and raw output; conversion errors can dominate the metric.}\note{Source: docs/ORB\_SLAM3\_OFFLINE\_PREPARATION.md; upstream pinned stereo\_inertial\_euroc.cc; evo Metrics/Formats. Commands are teaching examples only; none executed. UNKNOWN budgets require approval.}\end{frame}
