# Architecture / Research Decisions

Use this file for decisions that should not be reopened every session without new evidence.

Keep entries concise.

---

## ADR-001 — Pi vs STM32 ownership

**Status:** Accepted

**Decision:**

Raspberry Pi owns perception, VIO, SLAM and non-hard-real-time estimation. STM32 owns hard-real-time balancing, controller-side estimation and actuator safety.

**Reason:**

Robot balance must not depend on continued health of the Linux/ROS perception stack.

---

## ADR-002 — Camera IMU vs body IMU

**Status:** Accepted for Phase 1

**Decision:**

Use the D435i IMU for camera-centric VIO development. Keep the body IMU controller-owned. Do not begin naïve multi-IMU fusion.

**Revisit when:**

Independent frames, clock behavior, synchronization and calibration are characterized.

---

## ADR-003 — Upstream ORB-SLAM3 vs ROS 2 wrapper

**Status:** Accepted

**Decision:**

Treat official/upstream ORB-SLAM3 algorithm validation separately from ROS 2 wrapper integration.

**Reason:**

Wrapper/integration failures must not be confused with algorithm failures.

---

## ADR-004 — Evidence before gate promotion

**Status:** Accepted

**Decision:**

Compilation, a successful launch, or a visually plausible map is not sufficient to promote a gate to PASS.

---

## ADR-005 — Adaptive runtime progression

**Status:** Accepted

**Decision:**

Use the progression:

static characterization
-> rule-based policy
-> ablation
-> simple/contextual learned policy
-> reinforcement learning only if justified.
# ORB-SLAM3 offline preparation: IR1 + BMI085

Status: configuration review and build/input strategy prepared; **no build or
offline VIO run completed**. The camera session stopped at the platform power
gate. No new reusable image/IMU dataset exists. Calibration remains incomplete.
See [readiness](D435I_VIO_CALIBRATION_READINESS.md) and
[two-week gates](NEXT_TWO_WEEKS_PERCEPTION_PLAN.md).

## Source and prerequisites

The existing Mac and Pi ORB-SLAM3 checkouts both report commit
`4452a3c4ab75b1cde34e5505a36ec3f9edcdc4c4`. Mac submodule changes are untracked
`.DS_Store` files; they were preserved. No upstream source was edited.

Relevant code: `Examples/Monocular-Inertial/mono_inertial_euroc.cc`,
`RealSense_D435i.yaml`, `src/Settings.cc`, `src/Tracking.cc`, `src/Frame.cc`,
`src/ImuTypes.cc` and root `CMakeLists.txt`. The project's separate ROS2 wrapper
is not the input path for the first offline experiment. Introducing a first-party
runtime package, new build system or node graph requires architecture review.

Pi inventory: CMake 3.28.3, Eigen 3.4.0, OpenSSL development package present;
OpenCV development, Boost serialization development and discoverable Pangolin
missing. The RealSense ROS wrapper transaction would supply OpenCV; it does not
complete the remaining ORB build prerequisites. Recheck actual CMake package
discovery after installation. Do not compile under the current unstable supply.

The pinned CMake requires OpenCV >=4.4, Eigen >=3.1, Pangolin, Boost serialization,
OpenSSL, DBoW2, g2o and Sophus. It writes libraries/executables under the source
tree even with an out-of-tree build directory. Therefore use an isolated source
copy, not either preserved checkout. Its `build.sh` uses unbounded `make -j` for
some dependencies; invoke stages explicitly with bounded parallelism on a 4 GB Pi.
Pangolin is still required by this upstream build even for a future headless run.

Future build procedure after dependency/version review and stable power:

```bash
# On the chosen Linux build machine; choose a fresh local build destination.
WBR_ORB_SOURCE="$HOME/wbr-perception-phase1-runtime/third_party/ORB_SLAM3"
WBR_ORB_WORK="$HOME/wbr-offline-builds/orb-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)"
mkdir -p "$HOME/wbr-offline-builds"
mkdir "$WBR_ORB_WORK"
git -C "$WBR_ORB_SOURCE" archive 4452a3c4ab75b1cde34e5505a36ec3f9edcdc4c4 \
  | tar -x -C "$WBR_ORB_WORK"
cmake -S "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Thirdparty/DBoW2" -B "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Thirdparty/DBoW2/build" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Thirdparty/DBoW2/build" --parallel 2
cmake -S "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Thirdparty/g2o" -B "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Thirdparty/g2o/build" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Thirdparty/g2o/build" --parallel 2
cmake -S "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Thirdparty/Sophus" -B "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Thirdparty/Sophus/build" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Thirdparty/Sophus/build" --parallel 2
tar -xf "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Vocabulary/ORBvoc.txt.tar.gz" -C "$WBR_ORB_WORK/Vocabulary"
cmake -S "$WBR_ORB_WORK" -B "$WBR_ORB_WORK/build" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build "$WBR_ORB_WORK/build" --target mono_inertial_euroc --parallel 2
```

Run each step only after the previous succeeds, saving exact commands, complete
compiler logs, package/compiler versions and binary hashes. On failure inspect
the first actual error; do not change upstream algorithms or skip failures to
manufacture success. CMake/compiler compatibility fixes need an explicit patch
and review. The current upstream example creates a viewer: a headless display
or reviewed first-party driver is a remaining execution prerequisite.

## Configuration

[Candidate YAML](../experiments/2026-09-13-d435i-camera-capture-20260913T015621Z/orbslam3_ir1_bmi085_candidate.yaml)
contains this camera's 640×480 projection, 15 Hz requested image rate and the SDK
CAD camera-to-IMU transform. Comments classify SDK/factory-derived, source default,
temporary assumption and unknown values. No parameter is marked measured when
only enumeration exists. The four noise fields are deliberately nonnumeric;
they must be resolved before execution. Do not copy the upstream example's
different focal length, 30 Hz or noise values into this device's qualification.

`IMU.T_b_c1` is camera→body, as confirmed by `Frame.cc` composing `T_cb * T_bw`
and `ImuTypes.cc` constructing `T_cb = inverse(T_bc)`. SDK extrinsic arrays are
column-major, OpenCV YAML data row-major. Identity rotation in this snapshot
does not remove the need to test conventions for later measured calibration.

The settings path rescales continuous-time noise using `sqrt(IMU.Frequency)`.
Do not pre-discretize densities and then let the code discretize them again.
The 200 Hz candidate is a proposed gyro-grid input after accel interpolation,
not a claim that raw accelerometer samples arrive at 200 Hz. Time offset is
unknown; the candidate does not pretend it has been calibrated to zero.

## Recorded input and association strategy

Use finalized explicit-topic ROS2 bags when available. Preserve native SDK bags
separately: RealSense SDK recording files and ROS2 rosbag2 directories are not
interchangeable formats. Do not relabel a vendor frame-summary CSV as a dataset:
it contains no image pixels and rounds motion values.

Proposed offline conversion to the existing EuRoC reader's layout:

```text
derived_sequence/
  manifest.json
  association_metrics.json
  camera_timestamps.txt
  mav0/cam0/data/<original_timestamp_ns>.png
  mav0/imu0/data.csv
```

This is an adapter design, not an implemented or validated new project dataset
format. Before implementation review the format/API impact under AGENTS.md.
Keep originals immutable and derived data outside Git. The manifest must identify
input bag hashes, conversion source hash/commit, calibration/config hashes,
units/domains, interpolation rule, all rejected samples and clock-offset policy.

1. Decode each IR1 image without lossy compression or resizing; preserve mono8,
   resolution, source frame ID and exact integer ROS header nanoseconds. Save
   CameraInfo/extrinsics/TF separately and check that calibration stays constant.
2. Extract gyro and accel raw messages independently; preserve rad/s and m/s².
   Reject nonfinite, duplicate/backward stamps, unacceptable gaps or missing
   domains. Bag storage times are not substitutes for header stamps.
3. Define the common valid interval. For each gyro timestamp interpolate accel
   linearly between valid bracketing accel samples, with no extrapolation across
   a boundary or gap. Retain endpoints, bracket widths and interpolation fraction.
   This reduces representation mismatch; it does not measure synchronization.
4. Output EuRoC IMU columns `timestamp_ns,wx,wy,wz,ax,ay,az`. The pinned reader
   converts nanoseconds to seconds. Supply monotonically ordered image times and
   all appropriate IMU samples up to each image timestamp. Ensure leading and
   trailing IMU coverage; the upstream sample assumes valid boundaries.
5. If calibration estimates a time offset, record its sign convention and apply
   it exactly once in the derived association. Never rewrite the raw bag. Do not
   apply an additional SDK-axis rotation to already SDK-corrected motion blindly.

Adapter tests must cover interpolation on known linear signals, irregular rates,
gaps, duplicates/reversals, no extrapolation, exact nanosecond conversion,
transform inverse, lossless image roundtrip and message/count reconciliation.
The upstream live D435i example's interpolation helper overwrites the calculated
interpolation with the current sample; do not copy it as a validated reference.

Kalibr additionally needs a supported bag format and a measured target YAML.
Use its documented import/bag-creation path after exporting original images and
IMU; ROS2 bags are not accepted merely because the filename says “bag”.

## Evaluation and trajectory output

Future command after valid input/config/build/display prerequisites:

```bash
./Examples/Monocular-Inertial/mono_inertial_euroc \
  Vocabulary/ORBvoc.txt /path/to/qualified.yaml \
  /path/to/derived_sequence /path/to/derived_sequence/camera_timestamps.txt run_id
```

Use a new per-run working directory so trajectory outputs cannot overwrite an
earlier trial. The example calls `SaveTrajectoryEuRoC` and
`SaveKeyFrameTrajectoryEuRoC`; preserve both and verify nonempty finite output,
stamp ordering, coverage and coordinate convention. Record complete stdout/stderr,
exit/shutdown status, wall time, CPU/RSS, tracking-state timeline, initialization
time, reset count, per-frame processing delay, queue/drop counters where exposed,
and the full source/config/dataset identities.

Repeat fixed-data runs. Assess initialization and tracking continuity, then
trajectory plausibility against visible motion and known stationary intervals.
Use ATE/RPE only with suitable reference data and documented alignment; current
capture has no ground truth. Process startup or smooth output alone is not VIO
validation. No accuracy or performance improvement is claimed in this handoff.

