# First-party perception tooling

Tools live in [the native validation directory](../experiments/2026-09-12-pi5-native-sensor-validation/).
Mac is canonical; the Pi runs checksummed timestamped copies. SDK acquisition,
image processing, ROS recording and replay stay on the Pi. SSH is control and
post-run evidence transfer. Nothing here controls STM32, motors or balancing.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  M[Mac sources and tests] --> B[Immutable runtime bundle]
  B --> N1[N1 platform USB identity access]
  N1 --> N2[N2 smoke reproduction soak]
  N2 --> R[Raw logs CSV images health and review]
  R --> A[Reviewed N2 receipt]
  S[Qualified storage] --> N3[One ROS camera plus observer and recorder]
  A --> N3
  N3 --> D[Finalized explicit-topic bag]
  D --> P[Camera stopped: isolated replay and comparison]
```

An arrow is a prerequisite, not an automatic action. N1 requires current power,
USB and access evidence. N2 acceptance requires all three intervals including
300 seconds and explicit log/image review. Historical or synthetic data cannot
issue a physical PASS. Runtime receipts are host/boot/time/evidence bound.

| Tool | Purpose / input | Output / when used | What it proves | What it does not prove |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `n1_precheck.py` | Inspect platform, own USB branch, identity, idle ownership and normal-user permissions; physical availability/cable attestation | Raw USB/kernel/enumeration plus sealed `result.json`; before N2 | Current eligible USB/access/identity state if all checks pass | Sustained streaming, VIO calibration, storage speed |
| `phase_gate.py` | Enforce 20→105→300-second progression and reviewed acceptance; N1/previous receipts | Capture dispatch or `N2_ACCEPT` receipt | Complete sealed sequence and required review assertions | That a falsely asserted manual review is true; estimator accuracy |
| `run_sdk_capture.py` | Historical 2026-09-12 runner tied to the old USB UUID/path | Historical capture CSV/log/result | Context of the old experiment only | Current gate eligibility; do not use for new captures |
| `sdk_capture.py` | Own SDK/image/journal subprocesses; fresh N1, exact profile and bounded duration | Commands, CSV, images, health JSONL, package/binary hashes, automatic checks | Native capture/profile/timing/health and orderly shutdown within measured interval | Final N2 without reviewed soak; full image dataset; synchronized camera–IMU timing |
| `sdk_analysis.py` | Analyze vendor CSV against requested interval and stream thresholds | Counts, whole/interior rates, stamp/arrival gaps, frame discontinuities and boundary review | Integrity of recorded scalar timing/profile evidence | Pixel content, absent SDK timestamp-domain tags, precision lost by vendor CSV |
| `analyze_sdk_csv.py` | Historical CSV analysis used by earlier report | Historical JSON/terminal summary | Meaning of old analysis | Replacement for guarded current `sdk_analysis.py` acceptance |
| `image_content.py` | Parse representative PGM pixels plus sampler CSV | Dimensions, byte validity, intensity statistics and hashes | Saved samples have nontrivial structurally valid content | Whole-sequence image quality, intended motion or target detectability |
| `health_monitor.py` | Called by acquisition owner about once per second; optional child PID | Temperature, throttle flags, MemAvailable, CPU/RSS and free space | Sampled platform behavior during monitored coverage | Direct electrical power measurement; events shorter than sampling without kernel evidence |
| `kernel_analysis.py` | Classify raw SDK/kernel text without deleting it | Faults and attributable warnings | Known fault signatures detected in available logs | Absence of every possible failure; firmware correctness |
| `storage_qualify.py` | Pin external mount/source/UUID/identity; bounded sequential writes, fsync and readback | Throughput overall/worst batch, hashes, cleanup and sealed receipt | Measured margin on that exact external filesystem | Power-loss durability, cache-free reads or qualification of another mount; rejects microSD |
| `n3_observer.py` | Subscribe to specified topics with compatible QoS; live/replay/quiet modes | Counts, timestamps, payload hashes, frame IDs, camera/calibration/TF context | Observed ROS delivery over the measured window | Frames lost before publication, image-to-IMU physical synchronization, accuracy |
| `n3_record.py` | Require N1/N2/storage; inspect wrapper; launch exactly one camera, verify parameters, observe then record explicit topics | Live and recording results, finalized bag, clean shutdown evidence | ROS baseline behavior and stored topic/context integrity if accepted | MicroSD diagnostic authorization; it currently requires qualified external storage |
| `n3_bag.py` | Inspect finalized bag; verify no live camera; replay in isolated domain and compare | Bag content, count/type/stamp/payload comparison and replay receipt | Full stored-content replay within observed domains | Real-time capability, original acquisition correctness, VIO quality |
| `n3_metrics.py` | Pure common ROS topic/message metrics and comparisons | Stream/context validation and payload hashes | Consistent offline/live/replay content rules | Physical hardware behavior when inputs are synthetic |
| `bundle_runtime.py` | Copy allowlisted Mac tools and capture HEAD/dirty status/hashes | New bundle, manifest and SHA256SUMS; verify before Pi execution | Exact source identity of deployed utilities | Hardware PASS or clean canonical Git history |
| `validation_common.py` | Shared command capture, UTC, hashes, provenance, receipt/normal-user guards | Consistent evidence records and guard errors | Receipt scope/integrity/age/boot checks | Authorization from a CLI flag alone; signatures against a hostile editor |

Additional helpers: `sample_ir_checked.cpp` captures three PGM samples during a
separate 12-second image-only check; it does not extend the raw 300-second soak.
`platform_inspect.py` inventories software/network/storage without acquisition.
`wrapper_inspect.py` checks installed wrapper files/version and parameter readback.
`camera_metadata.cpp` reads current options, available intrinsics/extrinsics,
advanced-settings JSON and the active calibration table without starting streams
or writing camera state. Read failures remain in JSON and its exit is nonzero
for partial snapshots; metadata collection never issues N1/N2/VIO PASS.

## Ownership and limitations

Python runners own their child process groups and cleanup escalation. SDK owns
sensor threads; the image sampler owns its pipeline lifetime. Metadata export
is sequential and opens no streaming pipeline. ROS wrapper owns sensor capture;
observer and recorder are separate processes. Replay uses a separate domain,
after the live camera stops. No persistent network changes are needed.

The historical N2 CSV does not contain image pixels or timestamp-domain labels
and rounds IMU values. Store separate full-precision raw streams and domains for
calibration. Zero SDK noise variance is not measured zero noise. The current N1
guard rejects any sticky throttle bit; preserving history and establishing a
clean stable boot is the standard route. Fresh undervoltage is a real blocker.

The new task permits a separately assessed short microSD diagnostic bag. Existing
`storage_qualify.py`/`n3_record.py` deliberately implement the external-storage
research gate; do not forge a storage PASS to use that exception. A diagnostic
path would need explicit bounded evidence and must remain non-baseline.

## Build and verification

From the Mac repository root:

```bash
WBR_TOOLS="$PWD/experiments/2026-09-12-pi5-native-sensor-validation"
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest discover -s "$WBR_TOOLS" -p 'test_*.py' -v
WBR_BUNDLE="/tmp/wbr-runtime-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)"
python3 "$WBR_TOOLS/bundle_runtime.py" build "$WBR_BUNDLE"
python3 "$WBR_TOOLS/bundle_runtime.py" verify "$WBR_BUNDLE"
git diff --check
```

Deploy into a new directory under `/home/richard/wbr-runtime/`, then on Pi:

```bash
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest discover -s . -p 'test_*.py' -v
g++ -O2 -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra camera_metadata.cpp \
  -I/opt/ros/jazzy/include -L/opt/ros/jazzy/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu \
  -Wl,-rpath,/opt/ros/jazzy/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu -lrealsense2 -o camera_metadata
```

Preserve compiler warnings. Use the same compiler flags for
`sample_ir_checked.cpp`. No `colcon build` is needed for these standalone tools.
Use a fresh shell without `set -u` while sourcing Jazzy: the environment script
may legitimately read unset variables. The 2026-09-13 initial command exposed
this shell issue before enumeration; its log remains preserved.

Manual metadata check: after normal-user ownership and own-branch USB validation,
run `./camera_metadata --camera-available 243322073847 NEW_DIRECTORY`, save stdout,
stderr, UTC and binary hash. Parse every JSONL row; compare the selected Y8 profile
with full enumeration; inspect warnings and retained read errors. Exit 2 means
partial metadata, not success with missing values hidden. Never run as root.

Offline suite expectation at session start: 44 tests, one opt-in ROS integration
skip. `WBR_RUN_ROS_SYNTHETIC=1 python3 -m unittest test_ros_offline -v` on Pi checks
real ROS bag serialization/replay using generated data; this remains TOOLING ONLY.

