docs/DOCKER_RUNTIME_ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md-214-The service also specifies device-cgroup rules `c 81:* rmw` and `c 189:* rmw`: character-device major 81 covers video devices, and 189 covers USB bus devices. The flags allow read, write, and node creation at that control layer. Privileged mode already broadly relaxes device-cgroup restrictions. Neither setting rewrites the owner, group, or mode of a video node or an IIO sysfs attribute.
